  "notes": "USAGE:\nMore formal and solemn than {約束|やくそく}. Often appears in legal, religious, and ceremonial contexts. The compound {誓約書|せいやくしょ} (written pledge) is very common in business and legal settings.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {誓約|せいやく}を{交|か}わす (to exchange vows)\n- {誓約書|せいやくしょ} (written pledge; sworn statement)\n- {誓約|せいやく}を{守|まも}る (to keep a pledge)\n- {誓約|せいやく}に{違反|いはん}する (to violate a pledge)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {約束|やくそく}: promise — everyday, less formal\n- {誓|ちか}い: oath; vow — literary or ceremonial, often used in personal and religious contexts\n- {契約|けいやく}: contract — a legally binding agreement, more transactional than moral",
